# Monorepo

- Work inside a single top-level project: `cd <project-name>` before edits or package commands.
- Read that project’s `package.json` for scripts; there is no repo-root build or test.
- Match each project’s existing stack (React/Vite, plain HTML/JS, Maven, Python, etc.). Do not introduce new frameworks without an explicit user request.
- Conventions: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) (active focus + documented stacks). Full project catalog: [`.claude/rules.md`](../../.claude/rules.md).

## Boundaries

- Default project unless the user names another: see **Active focus** in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) (currently `chatbot-app/`). If the user path or request names a folder (e.g. `habit-tracker/`), work there — do not assume active focus.
- **Stack discovery**: `cd <project-name>`, read that folder’s `package.json` / README, and match what is already in the tree. Do not add frameworks the project does not use.
- **Skills**: Use `.cursor/skills/react`, `typescript`, `shadcn-ui`, and `tailwind-css` only when the target project’s deps or source already use that stack; use `design-system` for UI polish. Skip React/TS/shadcn skills for plain HTML/JS apps and path-scoped vanilla rules (`pokedex/`, `sql-learning-app/`). Projects not in AGENTS.md: see [`.claude/rules.md`](../../.claude/rules.md).
- Crew Orbit worker output goes under `/workspace/crew-orbit/` (outside this clone). Do not commit `crew-orbit/` if it appears locally (`.gitignore`).
- Run tests, installs, builds, or dev servers only when the user asks — not as automatic “verification” after edits.
